     "On 4 June 2026 Netflix released The Witness, a three-part drama about the murder of Rachel Nickell, told through her partner Andre Hanscombe and their son Alex, who was two when he saw the attack on Wimbledon Common. Both father and son advised on the series. The documentary The Murder of Rachel Nickell came out the same day. Their release, 34 years after the killing, put the Colin Stagg prosecution, the profile behind it and the missed chances to stop Robert Napper back in front of millions of viewers.",
